@startuml acknowledge-flow
title US-13: Acknowledge Flow - Operator Takes Ownership of an Alert

skinparam sequenceArrowThickness 1.5
skinparam participantBorderColor #555555
skinparam participantBackgroundColor #F8F8F8
skinparam noteBorderColor #AAAAAA
skinparam noteBackgroundColor #FFFDE7

queue "Kafka\nalerts" as Kafka
participant "Express API" as API
database "TimescaleDB\nalerts table" as TSDB
participant "Angular\nDashboard" as Dashboard
actor Operator

== Alert Created ==

Kafka -> API : consume alert event\n{ alert_id, entity_id, alert_type,\n  window_start_ms, payload }

API -> TSDB : INSERT INTO alerts\n( alert_id, entity_id, alert_type,\n  status, detected_at, payload )\nON CONFLICT (alert_id) DO NOTHING

note over TSDB
  alert_id = {entity_id}:{alert_type}:{window_start_ms}
  Idempotent insert - safe under Kafka replay.
  Initial status = NEW.
end note

API --> Dashboard : push new alert over WebSocket\n{ alert_id, status: NEW, entity_id, ... }
Dashboard --> Operator : alert appears in feed with status NEW

== Operator Acknowledges ==

Operator -> Dashboard : clicks Acknowledge on alert
Dashboard -> API : PATCH /alerts/:alert_id\n{ status: ACKNOWLEDGED }

API -> TSDB : UPDATE alerts\nSET status = 'ACKNOWLEDGED',\n    acknowledged_at = now()\nWHERE alert_id = $1

note over TSDB
  Idempotent - acknowledging an
  already-ACKNOWLEDGED alert is a no-op
  (no state change, no error).
end note

TSDB --> API : updated
API --> Dashboard : push status update over WebSocket\n{ alert_id, status: ACKNOWLEDGED }
Dashboard --> Operator : alert marked ACKNOWLEDGED in feed

@enduml
